## How It Handles the Requested Cases

**Hooks:** When the runnable's type equals `'hook'`, the starting node is taken from the hook's context via the currently running test rather than the runnable directly; otherwise the runnable itself is the starting node.

**Empty titles:** The loop only pushes a title when `node.title` is truthy, so empty or missing titles are skipped and won't appear in the resulting path.

**Ordering:** The traversal walks *upward* from the node through each `parent`, collecting titles from child toward ancestor. Because titles are gathered bottom-up, the function calls `.reverse()` at the end so the returned path reads from the outermost ancestor down to the innermost node.

